<title>UK: UK govt says Labour could not qualify for EMU.</title>
<headline>UK govt says Labour could not qualify for EMU.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Labour government would find it impossible to meet the convergence criteria to enable Britain to join a European single currency because of its spending commitments, Treasury Chief Secretary William Waldegrave said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Waldegrave was speaking at a Conservative Party news conference to launch a document claiming that pledges already made by Labour leaders would cost 30 billion stg a year to implement.</p>
<p>&quot;I think it would be completely impossible for them...to sign up for the single currency,&quot; Waldegrave said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 5427767</p>
</text>
